LLM integration (Free - No API Key Required):

The app supports three local/free LLM providers with automatic fallback:

1. **Ollama** (Recommended)
   - Download: https://ollama.ai
   - Start: `ollama run mistral`
   - Default model: mistral

2. **Jan** 
   - Download: https://jan.ai
   - Start: Open Jan desktop app
   - Default model: mistral

3. **GPT4All**
   - Download: https://www.nomic.ai/gpt4all
   - Start: `gpt4all-server`
   - Default model: mistral

**Setup:**
- Install any one of the providers above
- Run: `pip install -r requirements.txt`
- Start your chosen provider (or any of them - the app will auto-detect)
- No API keys needed!

**Optional:** Force a specific provider:
```bash
export LLM_PROVIDER=ollama  # (or 'jan' or 'gpt4all')
```

The app now exposes endpoints:
- `/run-llm-review` - Upload ZIPs, get logic-based review + LLM summary
- `/run-sharefile-review` - Download from ShareFile, get both analyses

Permanent deployment recommendation:

Use Railway or another HTTPS host instead of a local tunnel. This repo already has
`railway.json`, so Railway can run:

```bash
uvicorn server:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT
```

Set these production environment variables:

```bash
ADMIN_USER=your-login-user
AUTHORIZED_USERS=your-login-user
ADMIN_PASS=your-strong-password
SESSION_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://your-railway-domain.up.railway.app
LLM_PROVIDER=openai
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key
DEFAULT_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
```

Then configure the ShareFile API key/app redirect URI to exactly:

```text
https://your-railway-domain.up.railway.app/sharefile/oauth/callback
```

Use the top "Browser OAuth Login" form at:

```text
https://your-railway-domain.up.railway.app/run-sharefile-review
```

The callback URL shown in that form must match the ShareFile API app redirect URI.

Example request from curl:

```bash
curl -X POST "http://127.0.0.1:8001/run-llm-review" \
  -F "prior_zip=@prior_month.zip" \
  -F "current_zip=@current_month.zip" \
  -F "model=mistral" \
  -F "max_tokens=512" \
  -F "temperature=0.2"
```
